      "text": "It nests in horizontal holes warmed by geothermal heat. Foes who get too close can expect to be pounced on and bitten.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "It nests in small, horizontal holes in cave walls. It pounces to catch prey that stray too close.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives in caves warmed by geothermal heat. Even so, when the weather gets cold, it will huddle close with others of its kind.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It skulks in caves, and when prey or an enemy passes by, it leaps out and chomps them. The force of its attack sometimes chips its teeth.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It reacts to anything that moves—flies right at it and bites it. Sometimes it injures itself, but it doesn’t care too much.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its original home is an area much hotter than Alola. If you’re planning to live with one, your heating bill will soar.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gible prefers to stay in narrow holes in the sides of caves heated by geothermal energy. This way, Gible can stay warm even during a blizzard.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gible attacks anything that moves, and it drags whatever it catches into the crevice that is its lair. Despite the big mouth, Gible’s stomach is small.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "It nests in caves untouched by sunlight. Its sharp teeth may fall out when worn away or after an impact, but they regrow within a few days.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
